      "conditions": [],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1111,
          "quote": "One demonstrated failed admission obligation remains visible alongside a\ndifferent unresolved obligation. No sparse-publication allowance removes an\napplicable failed requirement. Publication proceeds only under the owning\nadmission predicate and authority, with tolerated ambiguity still reported.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL_METHOD.md#World%20Model%20Method%2FEntity%20Cut%20Construction%20Law%2FAdmissibility",
          "start_line": 1108
        },
        {
          "end_line": 1094,
          "quote": "An entity cut is admissible when its identity, boundary, authority, state,\nevidence, treatment, covariance, and ambiguity are explicit, traceable, and\ndiscriminated from plausible alternatives at evidence altitude proportional to\nthe claim.\n\nThat is the whole constitutional test. It binds what must be true of a\npublished cut. It does not prescribe how a builder establishes it.\n\n\"Explicit\" admits three lawful values on every surface: a stated value, stated\nabsence, or stated non-applicability with its reason. A cut whose entity has no\nadjacent-domain treatment says so; it does not manufacture one. This keeps the\npredicate whole without adding evidence machinery.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL_METHOD.md#World%20Model%20Method%2FEntity%20Cut%20Construction%20Law%2FAdmissibility",
          "start_line": 1083
        }
      ],
      "key": "entity_cut_admission",
      "statement": "Admissibility binds all eight surfaces—identity, boundary, authority, state, evidence, treatment, covariance, ambiguity—to explicitness, traceability and discrimination proportional to the claim. Explicitness permits a stated value, supported stated absence, or supported non-applicability with reason; missing treatment is declared rather than manufactured. The consumer binds the predicate and required evidence and conjoins component results. Unexamined properties remain unresolved; demonstrated failures remain visible alongside unresolved obligations. Publication requires the owning predicate and authority and reports tolerated ambiguity. This test does not prescribe a builder technique.",
      "uncertainty": "The referenced result-conjunction definition is not supplied."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["entity_cut"],
      "conditions": [],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1142,
          "quote": "Boundary is interventional in character, not structural. A cut that states its\nboundary only as a set of source fields has made a weaker claim than one that\nstates the reinterpretations under which identity survives, and should be read\nas such.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL_METHOD.md#World%20Model%20Method%2FEntity%20Cut%20Construction%20Law%2FDiscrimination",
          "start_line": 1139
        },
        {
          "end_line": 1118,
          "quote": "\"Discriminated from plausible alternatives\" means the cut states why this\nboundary rather than a nearby one the operating model would treat differently.\nThe claim carries its own discrimination; a stronger claim needs stronger\ndiscrimination.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL_METHOD.md#World%20Model%20Method%2FEntity%20Cut%20Construction%20Law%2FDiscrimination",
          "start_line": 1115
        }
      ],
      "key": "boundary_discrimination",
      "statement": "A cut states why its boundary differs from a nearby boundary the operating model would treat differently; stronger claims need stronger discrimination. Adjoint round-trip supplies semantic discrimination analogous to geometric boundary testing. Where intervention is possible, interventional evidence discriminates more strongly than declarative evidence, and the cut should identify its evidence kind. A field-set-only boundary is weaker than a boundary stating identity-preserving reinterpretations and should be read accordingly.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["entity_cut"],
      "conditions": ["An entity cut is published."],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1156,
          "quote": "A published entity cut makes the eight admissibility surfaces — identity,\nboundary, authority, state, evidence, treatment, covariance, and ambiguity —\nvisible and traceable, each as a stated value, stated absence, or stated\nnon-applicability, and records the basis on which identity was discriminated.\n\nCuts are immutable. Revising identity or boundary produces a new cut that\nsupersedes the prior one.\n\nConcrete carriers, layouts, schemas, and storage topology are consumer\nrealization. This method requires that the published surfaces survive; it does\nnot select the form they are stored in.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL_METHOD.md#World%20Model%20Method%2FEntity%20Cut%20Construction%20Law%2FPublication",
          "start_line": 1146
        }
      ],
      "key": "entity_cut_publication",
      "statement": "Expose all eight admissibility surfaces visibly and traceably as value, absence or non-applicability and record the identity-discrimination basis. Cuts are immutable; identity or boundary revision creates a superseding cut. Consumer-selected carriers, layouts, schemas and topology must preserve the published surfaces.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
