    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["markov_overlay"],
      "conditions": ["Before overlay publication."],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1284,
          "quote": "Assess uniqueness and transfer as separate predicates on the declared candidate,\nnull peers, contexts and representation, using the selected comparison and\nobservation rules. Evidence meeting each rule is satisfied for that predicate;\na demonstrated failure is falsified; an unrun or inconclusive comparison is\nindeterminate with actual performance retained. Invalid basis and established\nscope/capability shortfall retain their core diagnoses. Core size alone supplies\nneither failure nor success. Conjoin the required null-peer and treatment\nresults for overlay-publication eligibility, retaining failed comparisons and\nmissing coverage. That eligibility is distinct from ordinary entity-cut\nadmissibility and from formal conditional-independence closure.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL_METHOD.md#World%20Model%20Method%2FMarkov%20Object%20Construction%20Law%2F5.%20Null-Peer%20Discrimination",
          "start_line": 1275
        }
      ],
      "key": "null_peer_publication_gate",
      "statement": "Discriminate from incidental clusters using null peers. Core sizes overlapping null-peer sizes are expected and acceptable, never diagnostic. Identity-loaded core attributes should be unique among null peers and the direction should transfer more cleanly than a random representation diagonal. Failure on the required uniqueness/transfer tests prevents lawful Markov-object standing despite internally consistent invariants. Assess uniqueness and transfer separately against declared candidate, peers, contexts, representation and selected comparison/observation rules: meeting a rule satisfies; demonstrated failure falsifies; unrun/inconclusive comparison is indeterminate with performance retained; invalid basis and established scope/capability shortfall retain their diagnoses. Conjoin required null-peer and treatment results, retaining failures and missing coverage. Overlay eligibility is distinct from entity-cut admissibility and formal conditional-independence closure.",
