      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1346,
          "quote": "Builder projects may work a bounded source-object set repeatedly until the\nresulting attribute ledger is judged sufficiently saturated for publication.\n\nSufficient saturation means:\n\n- materially important attributes have traceable support\n- remaining gaps are explicit ambiguities rather than silent misses\n- the resulting object cut is stable enough to publish and supersede later if\n  needed\n\nSparse first publication remains lawful. Silent unsupported attribute creation\ndoes not.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL_METHOD.md#World%20Model%20Method%2FSaturation%20Law",
          "start_line": 1335
        }
      ],
      "key": "publication_saturation",
      "statement": "Construction is iterative; builders may revisit a bounded source-object set until judged sufficiently saturated. Saturation means traceable support for materially important attributes, explicit ambiguity for remaining gaps, and a cut stable enough to publish and later supersede if needed. Sparse first publication remains lawful; silent unsupported attribute creation does not.",
