      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1370,
          "quote": "A candidate geometric claim cannot acquire established standing through\ncomposition or averaging. Directions in different representation spaces do not\ncompose; changing that space supersedes the prior overlay. This domain policy\nadmits no generic translation exception. Claims of adjunction or equivalence\nrequire the evidence in [Orthogonal descriptions](FOUNDATIONS.md#orthogonal-descriptions).\n\nPrefer a federated world-model mesh to a flattened central model. Detailed\nmesh topology may remain product-local while the line is developed.\nMethod-level mesh law should be ratified only once the reusable node and edge\nmodel is stable; stability alone supplies no ratification authority.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL_METHOD.md#World%20Model%20Method%2FComposition%20Law",
          "start_line": 1361
        }
      ],
      "key": "world_model_composition",
      "statement": "Do not build a central monolith first. Compose local published artifacts/cuts under the library composition contract, binding participating cuts, exact bases, treatment predicates, fragment authorities, bounded-context meanings, declared loss and ambiguity; required checks conjoin actual claims. Higher-order publication retains local artifacts and identities. Composition/averaging cannot promote candidate geometric standing. Different-space directions do not compose; space changes supersede overlays. Adjunction/equivalence require referenced evidence. Prefer federation; topology may remain product-local during development. Method-level mesh law should await stable reusable nodes/edges, and stability grants no ratification authority.",
      "uncertainty": "Composition contract, core conjunction and Orthogonal descriptions are not supplied."
